# DianaSh golden corpus. Recorded from the C# shell, byte for byte, and frozen since its recorder went with the C# core host on 2026-11-07 - see EmuSen_DianaSh.md §13.4.
# Patterns: <ROOT> is the sandbox's real root, <TEMP> the corpus's real temporary folder, <INSTALL> the install's real directory;
# a 'match' block is a regular expression the whole output must match, written where a line prints a time or a measured number.
command useradd
usage 1   useradd <name>                add a new account (root only) - see `su`

case accounts
target none
covers 1
$ useradd tester
out 20
Added user 'tester'.
status 0
action none
$ useradd tester
out 33
useradd: 'tester' already exists.
status 1
action none
$ useradd
out 30
useradd: usage: useradd <name>
status 1
action none
$ useradd root
out 31
useradd: 'root' already exists.
status 1
action none
$ su tester
out 21
Switched to 'tester'.
status 0
action none
$ useradd other
out 33
useradd: only root can add users.
status 1
action none
$ echo $?
out 1
1
status 0
action none
end
